      "id": 1,
      "text": "Buffalo was named after the Buffalo Creek valley and served as a watering place for herds of bison.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buffalo%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Buffalo's founders required all buildings to be constructed of stone, helping many of the original structures survive over time.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buffalo%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town of Buffalo and its surrounding region were once part of the Louisiana Purchase of 1803.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.okhistory.org/publications/enc/entry?entry=BU004"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Buffalo became the county seat of Harper County and was officially incorporated in 1908.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
